From b9ddec58cdd964ed6125e6d8e567adb0e2547111 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:53:39 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(post): generic ISO wire EDM post - RS-274 motion,
 every EDM code from the machine's edm.codes

assets/posts/wire-iso.cps ("Generic ISO Wire EDM") posts the 2-axis Wire
Contour: G0 to the start hole, AWT thread (or M00 for the operator),
condition select and compensation cancel from .mch edm.codes, the
wire-centre path in G1/G2/G3 X Y with no F, then wire cut and tip
disposal. A missing required code refuses by name ("machine <m> states
no edm.codes.<x>"); a non-wire_edm machine is refused by name.

- post: Machine.edm_codes parsed from edm.codes (edm_codes.rs); the
  mirror and script_props expose machine.kind and machine.edm for EDM
  kinds; the engine refuses PARAM EdmCondition through a script without
  the wireEdm manifest flag.
- app: posting_wire streams the op's section (EdmCondition, WireSide);
  WIRE_POSTS, post_serves and default_post_for serve wire EDMs.
- tests: wire_post.rs with a synthetic fixture (fictional FX- codes) and
  the golden nc/wire-iso/wire_contour_punch.nc.

Not exercised on a real EDM control (#290 D10).

Fixes #533

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
